WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:16.299
I remember reading the first few chapters of my hero academia back in 2014

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:22.540
Naruto was coming to a close and the torch was about to be passed down to the next great shounen series

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:23.860
It's funny how both

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.160
Naruto and my hero academia have the inherited will of the next generation as a major theme

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.520
I think in reality

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.900
My hero academia has inherited a lot that the previous generation has developed and made it its own

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.320
in the same way deku

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.000
Inherited his powers from all might and is now making them his own too

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.990
I don't know whether this similarity is by accident or whether the author horikoshi is

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:51.699
Inspired by his own situation and is making a focal point of his series

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:52.570
Well

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.300
Hopefully some of these awesome moments

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.060
Are going to inspire you to get into the series or, if you've already watched the show,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.310
It will remind you of why you like it so much

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.000
Starting off at number 10 is the entrance exam's final moment

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.220
At the start of the show our main character, Midoriya, was pretty much a loser.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.360
In a world full of special abilities, he was a quirkless nobody

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.260
and to make matter worse: He wanted to be a superhero

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:34.140
It's like wanting to be a pro basketball player, but not having any arms

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:41.389
He's recognized for his courage by all might who, luckily for him, has the gift of being able to transfer his ability to another person

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:46.068
It's all about the hero's journey here: a lot of shounen shows start this way

00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:53.059
But then they get that one moment to shine and this was Midoriya's first "oh yeah, this is gonna be amazing" moment

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.660
At number nine we have All might versus Midoriya and Bakugou

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.160
Some lessons are learnt the hard way. The really hard way.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:30.720
Hit over the head hard, slammed in the ground hard, stepped on hard... The inspirational quote goes "Nothing in life hits as hard as life"

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.380
Well, I'm pretty sure All Might hits harder

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:38.180
I think this is one of those moments that made Bakugou one of the most popular characters in the show

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:45.720
His "I'm not gonna back down" attitude and "no matter what the difference in strength is, I'll destroy whoever I'm facing" mentality

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.400
Makes you love him, even though he's a massive prick.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.160
A massively lovable prick

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.400
Moving on to number eight we have Bakugou's rescue

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:30.619
This was a close one. A lot of us thought that we were gonna lose Bakugou here as well

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.130
Luckily for us, though

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:36.139
He's a badass that spits at the arm the Villains league extends to him

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:41.630
This arc starts off tense with the third villains League attack now bolstered by the new recruits

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.510
They kidnap Bakugou and try to recruit him

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:50.200
He gives them a "hell no" and then it all accumulates through an epic rescue orchestrated by Midoriya

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.320
The type that I would have perhaps wanted to see in another show 15 years ago

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.429
At number seven it's Stain's rage moment

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:14.070
Although All for one is stronger for most of us, Stains's the best villain of the show so far

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:19.200
I think we all just love people who don't back down when facing challenges larger than themselves

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.600
And characters that have strong consistent values. The hero killer's just like that.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.420
Sure, his goal was to murder a bunch of pro heroes, too

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:32.800
But he's doing it out of his own twisted desire to purge society of all the fake heroes.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.080
And it's still admirable how when faced against so many heroes

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.840
He doesn't back down

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.360
He even saves midoriya from a villain because he thinks he's someone who deserves to be a hero

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.860
When Endeavor, the second strongest hero, shows up does Stain run away?

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:47.360
No

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:55.080
He calls him a fake and starts walking towards him. That's the kind of attitude we all need to have just without the killing part

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:25.060
Next on the list at number six is when Todoroki uses his left

00:05:25.999 --> 00:05:31.059
Two things make this moment amazing for me. The first is Todoroki's personal growth

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:37.840
My hero academia has a diverse and well-made supporting cast and Todoroki is one of my personal favorites.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:45.060
He's someone with the most natural talent out of all of the next generation students and yet he suppressed his half of it

00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:47.069
Because of his relationship with his father

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:52.599
This is the moment where he gets over his inherited past and looks towards his own self-made future

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:55.748
The second is the mentality of Midoriya

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.840
He encourages Todoroki to use his full power to get over his mental issues and grow as a person

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:05.400
And this opposes his personal goal of the moment to win the match

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:11.340
But it serves the greater goal of having a peaceful world by helping the allies grow as heroes

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:43.200
At number five it's All for one's introduction.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.900
I'm really glad that in anime the villains are rarely overlooked

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.820
They play a crucial role in every series

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.480
and that's something I've covered in the top ten antagonists groups in anime

00:06:55.100 --> 00:07:00.580
A hero's only as strong as the villains he faces with the exception of One punch man, of course.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.240
The brighter the light, the darker the shade.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:06.431
All for one is the darkness to All Might's light.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.400
As much as All Might is loved, All for one is feared.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:14.600
His presence, powers and dark philosophy all accumulate

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:20.100
into one of the best and most chilling antagonist introductions I've seen in shounen anime

00:07:47.619 --> 00:07:51.479
Next on the list at number four is when Midoriya defeats Muscular

00:07:51.699 --> 00:07:55.558
While there doesn't seem to be any official power ranking in my hero academia

00:07:56.199 --> 00:08:00.988
Muscular was probably the most powerful opponent Midoriya faced up to this point in the show

00:08:01.899 --> 00:08:05.999
Midoriya was once again pushed far beyond his limits when trying to protect someone

00:08:06.249 --> 00:08:10.888
This characteristic of his was the reason why all might picked him as his successor

00:08:11.019 --> 00:08:17.129
We saw that he made the right choice when deku managed to put everything in his attack to defeat muscular against all odds

00:08:17.559 --> 00:08:22.078
It also shows why stain saved midoriya and thought he's worthy of being a hero

00:08:22.659 --> 00:08:27.029
Midoriya has consistently placed his own life in danger to save others from danger

00:08:27.029 --> 00:08:30.599
and in these moments is where he's always managed to shine the most

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.950
At number three, we have all might versus Noumu

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:09.009
The first attack of the league of villains was the first time we saw some organization on the villains part

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:12.180
The attack gave a lot of the students a chance to shine

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:17.580
Midoriya especially, but no one got as much of the spotlight in the attack as All Might

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.960
All might is a godlike figure that no one's been able to push at that point in the series (except for his own health)

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:30.060
Noumu, the artificial human made by one for all with the explicit purpose of defeating all might,

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:33.720
has the ability of shock absorption meant to counter All Might's strength.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.732
This epic fight gave us the first full extent of All Might's powers:

00:09:37.732 --> 00:09:40.599
both his physical strength and his mental fortitude

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:45.300
to overcome his own boundaries and push himself past his illness and limits

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:16.600
In second place it's the second fight between Midoriya and Bakugou

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:22.560
Unlike others who grew up with their quirks, refining them and making them stronger as they grow

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:28.320
One for all's already a full-grown quirk that's given to someone who has no idea how to use it

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.120
It's like giving a machine gun to a toddler

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:35.266
But then the person who received the one-for-all grows much faster than anyone

00:10:35.266 --> 00:10:36.860
So from Bakugou's perspective

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:43.730
It must be infuriating to see the weak boy he''s known since childhood has now caught up or might even overtake him.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.060
It's a lesson about not comparing yourself to others.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:50.240
While both of these boys have grown up in strength substantially

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.620
Bakugou is not looking at his own growth, but looking at Deku's

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.560
Instead of finding joy in his own growth he finds pain in the growth of his classmate

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.460
I wonder if endeavor had this moment with All Might

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:34.300
And finally at number one it's the United States of smash.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.900
All for one is the villain above all other villains

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:42.780
While in the show we're seeing a peaceful world where villains have retreated in a recent past

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.175
It wasn't always like this

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:47.640
At the start of the quirk era, crime used to rule society

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:53.620
At the top of this world ruled by villains stands all-4-one: the king of villains.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:57.680
The turning point of the world was probably when All  Might defeated All for One

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:02.300
He was the third One for All user (that we know of) to attempt this and the first to succeed.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:06.460
What we see in the show is a reenactment of their last fight years ago

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:10.640
That was probably the last time we got to see All Might at his full strength

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:11.840
And it was glorious.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:44.360
Well, thanks for watching and this time we are having a giveaway so leave a like and subscribe if you haven't already

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:48.259
And you might be the lucky person chosen to inherit All Might's quirk.

00:12:48.259 --> 00:12:50.320
I'll see you next time on Vinny tube.

